//! Orbit: three hotels and an office on the same site, from the scheme drawing (Office_Hotel_Layout.dxf, in the
//! site drawing's own coordinates). The drawing's linework is kept as drawn - facades, corridor lines, room
//! partitions, island and atrium outlines - and each building is fitted out over it:
//!
//! - Upper-scale Hotel (oval, the revised layout): eight rooms along the sides and four suites at the ends round a
//!   lens-shaped corridor; the island holds an atrium at each end, the core and a service room.
//! - ULO Hotel (oval): eighteen keys (45-76 m²) round a corridor ring; three atria, two service rooms, two cores.
//! - Midscale Hotel (the leaf): the drawing gives only its outline, so the layout is ours - keys 8 m deep along
//!   the facade, a corridor ring, an inner zone of back of house, core, atrium, core, back of house; the three
//!   sharp tips, too deep for a key, are guest lounges; slivers under 26 m² are linen stores, not keys.
//! - Office (horseshoe): the open-plan band, the corridor ring, the meeting hub (fitted with glass meeting rooms),
//!   the service spine (cut into WCs, risers and stores), the atrium, three cores.
//!
//! Each core block in the drawing is replaced by a code-width core in the same footprint: two lifts at the end the
//! drawing puts its lift shafts, a 2.8 × 5.6 m stair at the other, plant between. Every key gets a 2.4 × 1.9 m bath
//! on its corridor side, a door, a bed and a desk. Other uses on the site are the bubble diagram's, as context.
//! Coordinates are model millimetres on the site drawing (DXF minus the site origin 300000, 500000).

